# AmplifyUP — use the SDK, do not rebuild it

AmplifyUP SDK (`@amplifyup/sdk`) already owns layout resolve, Composer preview, Field/Slot/props context, personalization, page context, tracking, and the component-ID → render pipeline.

For placeable work, follow `.cursor/skills/amplifyup-placeables/SKILL.md`.

## Hard rules

- **Do not reimplement SDK functionality** in this repository (no parallel “Amplify framework”).
- **Do not create** local catalogs, registries, ComponentRenderer wrappers, placeable indexes, or duplicate Edge/resolve/preview/pageContext helpers.
- **Do not expand** `renderAmplifyComponent` into a registry system. That file is only the thin `renderComponent` callback `AmplifyPageContent` requires: map `component_id` → existing React placeable, wrap with SDK `ComponentContextProvider`, return.
- **Trust `fields` envelopes.** Placeables take `LayoutComponentProps<T>` and bind `<Field field={fields.x} />` (same for RichText/Image). Read with `fields.x.value`. Do not use removed `useComponentProps` or bare `value={live.x}` for schema fields.
- **One field per SDK binding.** Never `landscapeImage || mainImage` in `field={…}`. Use `isComposerPreview()` only to change display.
- Before adding Amplify infrastructure, **read current SDK types** (`@amplifyup/sdk/react`, `@amplifyup/sdk/server`). Prefer SDK exports over site-built equivalents.
- Site work for Amplify is: **placeable React components** (`Field` / `RichText` / `Image` / `Slot` / `isComposerPreview`) and **page wiring** (`AmplifyPageContent`, `fetchPageConfigServer`, provider `pageContext`).
- **Do not fix Composer/product bugs in this site.** Fix Composer/SDK or uptick the package.

## When adding a placeable

1. Content interface matches Composer field names.
2. Props: `LayoutComponentProps<Content> & Settings`.
3. Bind every editable field with `field={fields.…}` — no multi-field fallbacks.
4. Register `component_id` in Composer; one `renderAmplifyComponent` map entry.
5. Only null-check missing content when **not** in Composer.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const live = useComponentProps();
<Field value={live.title} />
const img = live.landscapeImage || live.mainImage;

// ✅ GOOD
export function ArticleDetail({ fields }: LayoutComponentProps<{ title: string; landscapeImage?: ImageValue }>) {
  return (
    <>
      <Image field={fields.landscapeImage} />
      <h1><Field field={fields.title} /></h1>
    </>
  );
}
```
